WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.934
-Peter Sarsgaard.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:04.734
I've known you for a long time.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.200
-We've known each other
for a long time.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.767
Yeah. Back in the day, with...
-Who were we hanging with?

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:13.334
-Julie Panebianco in the day.
-That's right. Julie Panebianco.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:15.067
-We met a lot of
very cool people.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.367
-I remember.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.000
Were you sleeping on
someone's couch or something?

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.834
-I was. You know,
Julie knew Michael Stipe.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.434
-Yeah, of course.
-She knew all
the cool rock stars.

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.434
I mean, we met
a lot of very cool people.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:29.033
And Michael had
an apartment above her

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:32.200
and he was redoing it,
so there was nothing in it.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.033
And she said, "You know,
I don't think he'd mind

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.200
if you stayed up there
for a little while."

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.400
-No way.
-So I stayed in that apartment

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.300
and I wanted to be respectful,

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.300
I remember, and I don't know,
it made sense at the time.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.901
So I pitched a tent
in the apartment.

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:46.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.133
He had no furniture, you know,

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.067
because he was going to
redo the apartment.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:52.767
-So you lived in a tent
in Michael Stipe's apartment?

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:55.667
-I did, and he had all of
this really nice wine.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:57.868
Well, I didn't know
it was really nice wine.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.200
So, you know, you come up
and you'd be like,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.601
"Well, I'll replace this one."

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.434
You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:08.200
Wait, was he ever there?

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.801
-Michael was never there.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.968
I got to know him
a little bit through Julie.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.100
You know, there'd be
parties and things.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.434
You'd see him around.
You and I, you know.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:17.601
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.133
-We shook our money
makers here and there.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.501
-I mean, we would hang out.
It was like

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.000
Michael Stipe and Bono.
-Bono.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.734
-I mean, come on,
both those guys together.

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.100
And you sit there
and you go like...

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.834
-Well, I was at a party
with the two of them together,

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:37.334
and it wasn't a very big party.
And somebody put U2 on,

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:42.033
and I have this thing I'm like,
"I'm an air guitarist."

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:43.667
-Oh.
-As we all are,

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.534
if we've had
a few too many drinks.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.033
-Yeah.
-And so I'm playing air guitar

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:53.067
to a U2 song with Bono, Michael
Stipe, not very far away.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:56.067
And I remember very clearly
that Michael kind of walked over

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.467
to me and just went...

00:01:58.534 --> 00:01:59.934
"No, no."

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:06.133
-"No, no, just no. Don't do it.
No, no, please.

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.267
Bono's right over --"

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.267
-It's very subtle.
He's like, "Peter. Peter.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.601
No, no."
-Yes, very quiet.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:14.033
In front of Bono.
-Insanely embarrassing.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.200
-I don't know if I've ever
seen you play air guitar.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.067
-My children have seen me
air guitar.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.434
-Would you air guitar right now

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:20.801
if the Roots played something
right now?

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:24.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:27.334
Just anything. You got a jam?
-Where's my light?

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:28.701
♪♪

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.234
Where's my light?

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:33.868
♪♪

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:35.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:37.300
♪♪

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.567
-Wow.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:59.267
♪♪

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.601
Wow!

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:06.067
♪♪

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:13.000
[ Laughing ]

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.200
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.067
He threw his guitar.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.000
He threw his guitar
and someone caught it.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.601
Thank goodness.
-That's my homage to Prince.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:22.334
-Thank you for doing that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.634
I don't ever want to make anyone
ever do anything on my show,

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:25.767
but that was fantastic.
Thank you for doing that.

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:29.000
-I could've gone on
for much longer.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.968
-Let's talk about
your new film, "Memory."

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:33.100
-Why not?
-You're getting great reviews.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.434
In fact, buddy,
you won Best Actor

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:38.434
at the Venice Film Festival.
Come on, that's not too shabby.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.567
Look at that.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.567
-That is a --

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:45.501
It's like they're
pranking you with this award.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.701
Do you see how big this is?
-Giant. Yes.

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.200
-I love this film.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.567
I loved it since I got it.
Jessica Chastain.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:55.667
-You were phenomenal.
Oh, you and Jessica Chastain.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.234
You know what I compare it to?

00:03:57.234 --> 00:04:00.200
It's like watching two --
It's like watching

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.267
Roger Federer
play Roger Federer.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:05.334
It's like two awesome
people at their best.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.267
And you're just so much fun
to just watch.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:10.467
Even though the subject matter
isn't the most fun thing,

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:11.601
but it's like two --

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:13.133
-No, I mean,
but here's the thing.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.701
It isn't the most fun thing.

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:18.200
Look, she has serious trauma
in her life

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.634
that she's dealing with.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.701
And I play a guy
with early onset dementia.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:25.434
So she's got all this stuff
that she can't forget

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:26.968
and I can't remember anything.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:29.901
-Yeah. It kind of fits.
-Actually a perfect couple.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:32.367
-It's a beautiful movie.
-She tells me about her trauma.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:33.801
Then the next day
we get together

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:36.734
and I don't remember any of it.
-Yeah, no.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:40.701
Yeah. It's just so -- You play
it so well. It's heartbreaking.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.734
It's beautiful.
It's well done.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.968
The director again?
-Michel Franco.

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.934
Yeah.
-It's -- Yeah.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.834
You'll love this movie.
I want to show a clip.

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.567
Here's Peter Sarsgaard
in "Memory."

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.467
Take a look at this.

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:59.667
-Hi. Welcome back.
Can I get you anything to drink?

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:03.367
-I'll have some water, please.
-The usual for you?

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:04.701
-Hm?
-The usual?

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:06.234
-Oh, yeah.
-Oh.

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.167
-What's the usual?

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:13.234
-I don't know.

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:15.000
-[ Chuckles ] You don't --
-No.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.934
-Do you remember her?
-No.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.801
-Okay.
-I don't think I know her.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:24.834
-But you do remember
that the food is good.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.434
-Oh, yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.200
-It's memorable.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:34.234
-Yeah. It's like, "The usual?"
"Yes, of course."

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:35.601
Peter Sarsgaard, everybody.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:37.934
"Memory" opens
in select theaters

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:41.801
December 22nd,
nationwide January 5th.

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:44.100
Chef Daniel Humm
joins us after the break.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.133
Stick around, everybody.

